A||||4||Wannabe||'88 Handling||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||05-19-2001||04:19 PM||||Amid the usual smirks, guffaws and puzzled looks of the other participants with their "Type Rs", 'Vettes, Hondas, Miatas Talons etc, I fanally got a chance to put all the hearsay about the '88 handling to the test nad find out if the long search for a good '88 Formula was worth the trouble. Fortunaltely, it was and I can say that the Formula is one of the best handling cars I have driven. In spite of being severly limited by the old, all season s-rated Cooper tires that were on the car when I picked it up two weeks ago, the car was well balanced and predictable. If anyone is interested, I'll post more details about the day and my experience, otherwise you can read about on the Fiero Racing List.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||05-19-2001||04:27 PM||||If you think it handles good now wait till you get good tires and renew the suspension!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||05-19-2001||07:16 PM||||Yeah I thought my 88 handled good before poly and KYB's.  Now that I have those it's really great.  Next is front/rear coil overs so I get rid of that wheel gap.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Fformula88||05-19-2001||10:55 PM||||I'm not sure the Fiero will severely out handle some of the cars you mention, but it can certainly hang with most of that group.  Get some new shocks/struts at all four corners and a good set of tires and hang on for the ride!||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||05-20-2001||07:59 PM||||I test drove a 88 coupe last month, i wish i had the money for it. it didnt plow it was smooth i loved it||||reg||1
